-- Migration 4 -> 5: switching a plan without losing what came before.
--
-- The billing cycle is a column on the subscription, not a versioned table like
-- price_periods, so every occurrence is recomputed from the anchor using
-- whatever cycle is current. Editing monthly to yearly therefore reshapes months
-- already paid: a 10.99 charge in July silently becomes 89.99, and the months
-- between vanish. Correct history needs two records -- the old plan ended, the
-- new one anchored where it starts.
--
-- Two records is right for the data and wrong for the person, who has one
-- subscription to F1TV and expects one row. `replaces` reconciles the two: the
-- new record names the one it supersedes, so the pair can be stored separately
-- and presented as a single continuing subscription.
--
-- Held on the NEW record rather than as `superseded_by` on the old one, because
-- it is written once at creation and never touched again. The other direction
-- would mean editing an old record every time the plan changed, and each edit is
-- a fresh chance for two devices to disagree about it.
ALTER TABLE subscription ADD COLUMN replaces TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '';
